<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Shops</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>list</a>
buy &lt;item&gt;
buy &lt;number&gt; &lt;item&gt;
sell &lt;item&gt;
value &lt;item&gt;
request &lt;item&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>list
buy bread
buy 3 bread
value sword
sell sword
</pre>
<p>In a shop, the shopkeeper trades with you:
</p>
<ul><li><b>list</b> shows what is for sale, and the prices.</li>
<li><b>buy</b> buys a thing, or several of it at once. Any coins will do: you get</li></ul>
<pre> your change back.
</pre>
<ul><li><b>sell</b> sells one of your things to the shopkeeper.</li>
<li><b>value</b> tells you what the shopkeeper would pay for one of your things,</li></ul>
<pre> without selling it.
</pre>
<ul><li><b>request</b> asks the price of a thing for sale.</li></ul>
<p>Shopkeepers only buy the kinds of things they trade in, and only while they have 
money left. As in real life, some charge more and some pay more than others, so 
it can pay to shop around. A shop's stock runs out, and is filled up again day 
by day.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Money</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help List</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Request</a>
</pre>




</div>